Applied 95 repository migrations (0001 - 0098) on PostgreSQL 17.11.
PASS split cancel: a second session WAITS for the first, then credits nothing (no double refund)
PASS split cancel: the first session ROLLS BACK, the waiting session then performs the whole refund
PASS split cancel: 16 simultaneous sessions (retailer, admin, service) refund exactly once
PASS opposite entry points at once (whole order, child A, child B, legacy status RPC): no deadlock, exact totals - 25 rounds
PASS two admins close the two children at the same moment: parent cancelled once, coupon released once
PASS partial failure under concurrency: a failing session changes nothing and does not poison the next one
PASS a direct status write racing the atomic call is refused; the atomic call still completes
PASS snapshot: assigned staff cannot rewrite quantity_ordered / order_item_id / delivery_id, delete or forge a line
PASS snapshot race: completion holds the delivery; a concurrent staff quantity write WAITS and is then refused
PASS snapshot race: a staff quantity write in flight makes completion WAIT, and completion then re-checks the committed quantities
PASS snapshot: refund and loyalty use the original order quantity end to end (Rs 1,000 / 10 pcs, 2 missing -> Rs 200 and 8 points)
PASS marketplace switch: two Super Admin sessions are serialised; the later decision wins; history keeps both
PASS seller gate holds for every role on real PostgreSQL (switch off, then on without acceptance, then accepted)
